\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \emph  {Top:} the model. The encoder never changes the length, so every downstream quantity keeps a time axis. The head's two branches multiply into the evidence $g_j^k$, the single quantity from which \emph  {both} outputs are read: the prediction is a reduction of it over time, the interpretation \emph  {is} it. \emph  {Bottom:} the change inside the block --- the pointwise $1\times 1$ channel mix is factorised through a narrow middle layer, halving the term that dominates the parameter count.}}{4}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{2}{4}{\emph {Top:} the model. The encoder never changes the length, so every downstream quantity keeps a time axis. The head's two branches multiply into the evidence $g_j^k$, the single quantity from which \emph {both} outputs are read: the prediction is a reduction of it over time, the interpretation \emph {is} it. \emph {Bottom:} the change inside the block --- the pointwise $1\times 1$ channel mix is factorised through a narrow middle layer, halving the term that dominates the parameter count}{figure.caption.7}{}}
